rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-SESSION.md:235:### Production native monitor/command oracle (2026-10-28; adapters remain open)
rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-SESSION.md:239:The real monitor authenticates as a native uncoded person through genuine login work and receives both Test and `testGroupMonitor` claims. Admin/Login/ordinary participant credentials cannot send monitor commands; foreign people cannot poll or acknowledge another person's Test. `PUT /monitor/command` deduplicates addressed Tests, shares one command ID across them and converts arguments to PHP strings. Its frontend sends seconds (`Date.now()/1000`), explicitly truncated by the backend; this differs from the arbitrary int64 client clocks retained by Testlog. Queue reads are ordered by that supplied second timestamp. GET query parameters are ignored, while JSON-body `lastCommandId` applies a scoped strict timestamp comparison excluding equal-clock commands; an unknown scoped ID produces an empty queue, integer0 means no filter and a string ID returns500. ACK is scoped and idempotent, with exact reasons `OK` and `OK, was already marked as executed`; unaddressed command/Test pairs return404. Delivery, polling and ACK remain possible while the Test is locked.
rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-SESSION.md:254:This private persistence stage supplies the later native monitor authentication without placing credentials in public migration candidates. Command delivery/ACK and additional operational modes remain separate implementation work. No complete functional or visual parity row closes.
rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-SESSION.md:263:SQLite77/PostgreSQL71 store an explicit native operational person mode. Monitor people never default to a participant execution mode. Existing native people, first suffix, content binding and Test identity survive reentry and participant/monitor role changes; mode projection does not rewrite answers, state clocks, opening times, controllers or timers. Delayed parent/Run saves cannot restore a preceding mode. The new column is transactional and starts unknown for old rows; authentication resolves current private provenance without fabricating historical stored roles. All older schema test resets drop the new column while retaining their original assertions.
rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-SESSION.md:265:The native AccessSet matches actual Source65, including its raw physical Booklet label, Test claims collected from coded participant members of the monitor's authored group under empty code, `testGroupMonitor` claims/access, empty monitor flags and absent default view settings. The monitor owns distinct real native Tests and reads the honest `monitor-group` mode without canonical controller entry. Real SQLite and PostgreSQL HTTP tests solve configured work, reject direct credentials, invalid work, replay, wrong token types and foreign ownership, and verify the native mode. The visible Chromium protocol keeps every13 previous checks and adds a14th native monitor check using actual browser WebCrypto and the same owned protected API. Its request-specific Source lock constructor500 remains the sole expected server failure, with zero unexpected failures and owned API shutdown.
rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-SESSION.md:284:Tenant, workspace, native monitor role, group binding and recipient group are rechecked inside the write boundary. Source's global Test-existence check does not grant cross-group/workspace access: out-of-scope targets return404, retaining Rewrite's isolation boundary. Test/parent deletion removes deliveries without resetting the counter. Deleting only the commander nulls its audit reference and preserves recipients' packets. Production HTTP tests, actual late SQL insert failures, File publication failure, migration rollback/restart and deletion controls cover these paths across all four stores. Every historical migration assertion is retained byte-for-byte after the new table-drop prefix.
rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-SESSION.md:286:The protected visible-browser scenario retains all14 prior markers and adds shared delivery/locked-recipient and scoped/idempotent ACK checks. Its actual Original UI iframe keeps its running controller, unit responses and timers. Exactly one request-specific Source lock constructor500 is expected; unexpected server failures remain forbidden. These checks qualify transport beside the existing UI. Native frontend producer/poll/apply/ACK adoption, complete monitor UI, study/system-check authentication, additional operational memberships/settings, native monitor session lists, live broadcast and all8 broad visual rows remain open. No broad functional or visual row closes.
